      "title": "South African women condemn death sentence against Varisheh Moradi, call for an end to executions",
      "description": "Abahlali baseMjondolo (AbM), one of the largest grassroots movements to emerge in South Africa following the end of apartheid, issued a message of solidarity with Kurdish political prisoner Varisheh Moradi. Women members of the movement condemned the Iranian regime’s renewed death sentence against Moradi, issued on October 14, 2026, and called for the execution to be halted. In a visual message featuring numerous AbM members, the movement called on the Iranian regime to end its policies of repression and executions targeting Kurds. The message demanded the immediate release of Varisheh Moradi and all other political prisoners, while expressing solidarity with the women’s freedom struggle in ",
